{
 "_about": "FEED's half of the feed's one file (FEED lane 23, row [the feed is alive], rule 215(f): FEED owns the triggers, the pacing and the file; WORDS writes the lines). tools/bohemia_feed_build.py joins this with WORDS' bank (banks/BOHEMIA_WORDS_THE_FEED_BANK.json: the accounts, the handles, the lines with their Spanglish twins, the replies, the follow-ups, the faction plurals) into records/target/bb/feed_kinds.json, the one file the game reads at boot. Edit here for WHEN and HOW OFTEN; edit WORDS' bank for WHO and WHAT IS SAID; then run the tool. The kinds below marked _feed are FEED's own drafts for moments WORDS has no row for yet (WORDS may take any of them).",
 "pace": {
  "_why": "A real local feed: a handful of posts in a stretch of the day, more after something big, never a wall. MEASURED 10/26 on the demo's map: an in-game hour passes in 2.3 s of travel on dirt and 4.6 s on a road (10.75 game minutes a block, 1.22 blocks a beat), and the clock stops in towns, fights and when he stands still. So the window is four game hours, not one (a handful an hour would be two posts a second while he travels), and real_gap_s keeps one post on the glass long enough to read it. WORDS Q15 measured 30 neighbourhood feeds: about 1.4 replies a post, and the most common post is somebody asking for something.",
